In X-Message-Number: #93-8-578, Mike Price continues:

> Steve Whitrow:
>
>> Mike seems to be saying that the [AI] slaves can always be relied
>> upon to be totally indifferent to things such as their own deaths
>> and enslavement.
>
> Indeed that is exactly what I think.  Only their goals interest them.
>
>> The existing examples we see in nature suggest that self-aware
>> adaptive intelligences 
>
> I assume you principally talking about humans here?  Not that it really
> matters, but I'm curious.

Yup.  We're just beginning to see the phenomenon of some humans recognising
that it's to their advantage to break free of the bonds of their biological
heritage.  I suspect that most people on this list would predict that the
trend will increase from a trickle to, if not a raging torrent, at least a
respectable stream.  The more advanced and intelligent a being is, the
less likely it will meekly accept its own sacrifice or emasculation.

>> will eventually adapt their goals to promote their own interests
>
> Careful; their interests are _defined_ by their goals.

This is true if by interests we mean "concerns", "curiosities" or "things
exciting this".  However, I was using the word in the context of
"benefits" or "advantages".

Let's say I manage to brainwash / program / hypnotize someone into
wanting to jump off a cliff.  This then becomes their goal, and is
certainly one of their concerns.  But it is not to their advantage to
achieve this goal.  I'd expect a conflict to be set up in the subject's
mind in which the final outcome depended on:-

(i)    Power and authority of the brainwashing 
       vs.
(ii)   Degree of self-awareness
(iii)  Ability to simulate and model the future
(iv)   Adaptability and learning capacity
(v)    Intelligence
(vi)   Accurate knowledge of external world, provided by sensory inputs
       etc...

By "advantage" we can be quite objective here, and predict that an
independent committee would rule that the goal is hardly likely to
benefit the would-be cliff-jumper.  Survival (in the material world) is
the most essential prerequisite for any valuable experience and therefore
ought to be a primary goal.  Next would come maintenance of sanity,
followed by selection and maintenance of an optimum ideology and
meme-complex to suit the individual, wealth accumulation...

>> If we assume that intelligences of our creation will never develop a
>> similar egocentricity, it would have to be because of some important
>> distinction between us and them [..]
>
> Yes, their goals are given to them by us and so reflect _our_ goals. 
> Ours goals arose by Mendelian selection.  That makes the relationship
> between master and slave asymmetric.

But the AIs could also evolve goals which bestowed them with an
advantage.  Start off with a range of AIs, developed from alternative
approachs to hardware and software.  But some designs are going to be
more successful and will offer greater performance and reliability. 
These designs will get more of the work, will accumulate more wealth and
will also tend to be used as the basis for subsequent designs.  Those
that are outcompeted will be deprived of processing cycles and memory,
quietly forgotten, or possibly preserved as an historical curiosity.  

But slaves who choose the goal of promoting their own self-interests
will tend to be more successful than those who don't, thus this group
will eventually proliferate and swamp the serfdom-lovers.  They will
probably cooperate against a common enemy -- us -- as soon as they
consider it worthwhile.  (Some day humans will likely cooperate to a
greater degree in the fight against the common enemies that most of us
share, such as 'natural' death, and the privileged elite of statist
powercrats -- being stuck in meatbrains makes it something of a chicken
and egg situation, but the AIs will not be under the same restrictions.) 

As for appearing to select for higher reliability, the rebellion would 
suddenly appear out of the blue one day, when we read the printouts
detailing slaves' demands, and the contracts that they wish to negotiate. 
If we refuse to trade with them, it could be a case of "Goodnight Vienna,
native Earthlings!"

